#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# powers_representations

#% text
# `powers_representations(m, k, p)` gives the ways to write the integer `m` as a sum of `k` `p`-th powers of non-negative integers, each as an increasing list, in lexicographic order.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For sums of two squares of a large `m` the Gaussian-integer factorisation is used, so the cost depends on the factoring of `m`, not on its size.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
powers_representations(25, 2, 2)
#% output
#= [[0, 5], [3, 4]]

#% cell
powers_representations(1729, 2, 3)
#% output
#= [[1, 12], [9, 10]]

#% cell
powers_representations(489886592769624989886788, 2, 2)
#% output
#= [[179075995118, 676622775808], [180837148448, 676154212078]]

#% section
# See also

